WEBVTT

00:09:29.356 --> 00:09:32.401
looking at how Wikipedia writers
take on the most contentious

00:09:32.443 --> 00:09:33.611
and difficult topics.

00:09:34.028 --> 00:09:35.779
And what they found

00:09:35.821 --> 00:09:38.907
was that the system
actually works really well.

00:09:38.949 --> 00:09:41.577
These are some of the best
articles on Wikipedia.

00:09:42.119 --> 00:09:43.954
And many of them are written by people

00:09:43.996 --> 00:09:46.123
who fundamentally disagree
with one another.

00:09:46.957 --> 00:09:49.043
They also found something interesting,

00:09:49.043 --> 00:09:52.755
which is that the more
that these polarized contributors

00:09:52.796 --> 00:09:55.090
engaged in conversation,

00:09:55.132 --> 00:10:00.179
the more balanced and productive
their contributions became.